# The product of two bounds of intervals with 2-limb bounds, enclosed between two canonical 2-limb
# values l and h (milestone2.md, "Interval kernels", "Two limbs"). The operands are canonical and
# not NaN. A zero operand gives zero whatever the other one (0 times infinity is 0, the product of
# two bounds in interval arithmetic); otherwise an infinite operand gives the infinite product, as
# both values; otherwise mul_dir_2_2, and a value of it that is not finite becomes the infinity on
# its side (-inf for l, +inf for h), which is always a bound. For finite operands and a finite
# value the claims of mul_dir_2_2 hold of it, with its constants: on its side of x y, within
# A |x y| + B, normalized.
kernel:        mul_ext_2_2
input:         x = x0 x1
input:         y = y0 y1
output:        l = l0 l1
output:        h = h0 h1
value:         x*y
requires:      canonical x
requires:      canonical y
requires:      not_nan x
requires:      not_nan y
ensures:       normalized l
ensures:       normalized h
ensures:       outward l below rel=(2*(1+u)^3*up((1+u)^6)*up(unit(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2)))+2*u^2)*(1+unit(mul_2_2))/(1-u) abs=2*(1+u)^2*(1/2*up((1+u)^6)*eta+up((1+u)*(2*(1+u)^5*eta+tiny(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2))+eta/2)+eta/(2*u)))+eta+(2*(1+u)^3*up((1+u)^6)*up(unit(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2)))+2*u^2)/(1-u)*tiny(mul_2_2) zero_factor
ensures:       outward h above rel=(2*(1+u)^3*up((1+u)^6)*up(unit(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2)))+2*u^2)*(1+unit(mul_2_2))/(1-u) abs=2*(1+u)^2*(1/2*up((1+u)^6)*eta+up((1+u)*(2*(1+u)^5*eta+tiny(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2))+eta/2)+eta/(2*u)))+eta+(2*(1+u)^3*up((1+u)^6)*up(unit(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2)))+2*u^2)/(1-u)*tiny(mul_2_2) zero_factor
min_precision: 4
source:        mul_dir_2_2, with the products of a zero and of an infinity selected (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeIntervalMul2.v mul_ext_2_2_correct
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   every output is selected after explicit tests of the operands and of the finite results

(c0, c1, e0, e1) = mul_dir_2_2(x0, x1, y0, y1)
t   = prod(x0, y0)
ax  = abs(x0)
fx  = lt(ax, const inf)
ay  = abs(y0)
fy  = lt(ay, const inf)
fo  = and(fx, fy)
zx  = eq(x0, 0)
zy  = eq(y0, 0)
zz  = or(zx, zy)
nz  = not(zz)
ac  = abs(c0)
fc  = lt(ac, const inf)
ae  = abs(e0)
fe  = lt(ae, const inf)
mi  = neg(const inf)
p0  = select(fc, c0, mi)
p1  = select(fc, c1, 0)
q0  = select(fe, e0, const inf)
q1  = select(fe, e1, 0)
r0  = select(fo, p0, t)
r1  = select(fo, p1, 0)
s0  = select(fo, q0, t)
s1  = select(fo, q1, 0)
l0  = select(nz, r0, 0)
l1  = select(nz, r1, 0)
h0  = select(nz, s0, 0)
h1  = select(nz, s1, 0)
